    <!-- Ironpass ram cavalry (#515): 2.0 from level 21, and the level-41 marshal pays 3.0 under
         the level rule like every other listed troop. Until #585 the whole branch sat flat at
         2.0 on the argument that no mounted line escalated with tier (warg riders are 2.0 from
         level 11 to 36); the level rule now overrides that for any mounted troop at 41+, which
         also lifts the Black Numenorean knight and temple knight, the noldorin lancer, the
         rider of Himring, the Imladris horse archer and outrider, and Khamul's knights. 2.0 is
         double the Ironpass foot peers (infantry/axeman/veteran_axeman/mountain_guard, all
         unlisted at 1.0), the same ratio warg riders carry over orc infantry.

         ironpass_ram_herder (16) is deliberately ABSENT and falls through to the 1.0 default.
         It is the pooled branch root, so it is the rung a player recruits over and over from a
         notable, and a 2.0 entry unit would deflate the party-size limit for exactly the players
         this branch is meant to reach. It carries the light barding from 2026-09-06 (the ram's
         saddle is part of that mesh, so an unharnessed ram rides bareback), but the reason
         for the 1.0 is recruitment economics rather than armour, so the entry stays out.
         The 2.0 rungs start paying at 21. -->
    <TroopWeight id="ironpass_ram_rider" weight="2.0" />
    <TroopWeight id="ironpass_goat_charger" weight="2.0" />
    <TroopWeight id="ironpass_ram_breaker" weight="2.0" />
